# Preserved history is hash-locked: `losscolumn history verify` re-hashes every
# file under artifacts/history and compares it with the digest recorded when the
# artifact was withdrawn. Git's end-of-line normalisation rewrites those bytes on
# checkout, so a clone would get content that no longer matches its own digest.
#
# Found by scripts/reproduce.sh, which is the only place it can be found: in the
# working tree the file and its digest agree, and they stop agreeing exactly when
# somebody else clones the repository to check the claim. A preservation
# guarantee that only holds on the author's disk is not one.
artifacts/history/** -text

# The same reasoning applies to anything else carrying a recorded content hash.
artifacts/prereg/** -text
